pawlak@vxdesy.desy.de writes:
>I had a big problem, when the wizard managed to bring my bag of holding
>from 'blessed' to 'cursed' status in one turn. I immediately became
>'overtaxed', had to see 10 or so attacks. Plus, it can happen, that
>the cursed bag of holding will eat your holy water, so you'll not be 
>able to bless it back (I usually try to have at least two bags with me
>and carry holy water in both, just to avoid such type problems - in that
>game I had just one bag, but luckily the holy water survived). Anyhow,
>it is a very unpleasant curse...  


simple solution to this inevitable problem...
carry with you a sack to place critically important items to always have
in a not cursed state... ie extra unicorn horn, blessed remove curses, holy
water and, of course, your blessed bag of holding.  This way the wizard cannot
curse the items in the sack, only the sack itself, which unless I am mistaken,
will not cause any personal suffering. Ergo, your blessed bag of holding can
never become cursed, albeit items in the bag require a few more keystrokes to
access.

